  "task": "Identify distinct workloads (applications) running in AWS region eu-west-1, as the first step of a disaster-recovery readiness assessment. Do NOT assess DR posture yet — this is purely workload discovery/mapping.",
  "context": "User asked how well 'our workloads in eu-west-1' would survive a disaster. No specific workload was named, so per the DR assessment methodology we must first find candidate workloads before assessing any one of them. Look for: CloudFormation stacks in eu-west-1, AppRegistry/myApplications applications, resource groups, and tag values (e.g. Name, Application, Project, Environment tags) shared across multiple resources that suggest a logical application grouping. Also note any shared/common infrastructure (e.g. shared VPC/network stacks) that is NOT itself a standalone workload.",
  "resources": ["region: eu-west-1"],
  "timeframe": "current state, not time-bounded",
  "criteria": "Return a list of candidate workloads found, for each: name, how it was identified (stack name / tag / resource group), and its main resources (compute, data stores, entry points) at a high level. Do not go deep on DR configuration details yet (no backup/replication/AZ checks) — just enumerate and group resources into workload candidates. If a resource or stack appears to be shared infrastructure used by multiple workloads (e.g. a shared VPC), flag it as shared rather than its own workload."
}", "deep_research": false}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Discover candidate workloads in eu-west-1 via CloudFormation stacks, tags, resource groups"}], "created_at": null}

